{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "באשמורת הבוקר", :translit "b'ashmoret ha-boker", :gloss "at the morning watch"} {:he "ויבאו בתוך המחנה באשמורת הבוקר", :translit "va-yavo'u b'toch ha-machaneh b'ashmoret ha-boker", :gloss "and they came into the midst of the camp at the morning watch"} {:he "עת רצון", :translit "et ratzon", :gloss "a time of favor"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["באשמורת הבוקר" "ויבאו בתוך המחנה באשמורת הבוקר"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'b'ashmoret ha-boker' occurs in 1 Samuel 11:11 when Saul comes to rescue Jabesh-gilead, and in Exodus 14:24 at the splitting of the sea. Yoma 29a states that the last morning watch is a time of divine favor.", :sources ["Yoma 29a" "1 Samuel 11:11" "Exodus 14:24"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וישקף", :translit "va-yashkef", :gloss "and He looked out"} {:he "וישקף על פני סדום", :translit "va-yashkef al p'nei s'dom", :gloss "and He looked out over the face of Sodom"} {:he "וישקף אבימלך", :translit "va-yashkef avimelech", :gloss "and Abimelech looked out"} {:he "וישקף ארונה", :translit "va-yashkef aravnah", :gloss "and Aravnah looked out"} {:he "וירא את המלך", :translit "va-yar et ha-melech", :gloss "and he saw the king"} {:he "את הכל נתן ארונה המלך למלך", :translit "et ha-kol natan aravnah ha-melech la-melech", :gloss "all this Aravnah the king gave to the king"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["וישקף" "וישקף על פני סדום" "וישקף אבימלך" "וישקף ארונה"]}], :frame {:text "Genesis 19:28 records Abraham's 'va-yashkef' over Sodom's destruction by fire and brimstone. Genesis 21:16 and 26:8 identify Abimelech as king of the Philistines. 2 Samuel 24:23 records Aravnah's statement giving all to the king.", :sources ["Genesis 19:28" "Genesis 21:16" "Genesis 26:8" "2 Samuel 24:23"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ויהם", :translit "va-yahom", :gloss "and He threw into panic"} {:he "ויהם ה' את סיסרא", :translit "va-yahom Hashem et sisra", :gloss "and the LORD threw Sisera into panic"}]